  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only PCA with multiprofile and avgpool is the strongest setting so far (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), outperforming RNA single-profile (0.485) and multiprofile transformer aggregation (0.519), while image-only ResNet models are much weaker. The main uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve over PCA without changing the already-promising profile and aggregation choices. config_005 tests scvi_n200 with the same multiprofile avgpool setup, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the current best direction while efficiently reducing uncertainty about representation before moving to more complex multimodal or fusion experiments."
